From: Kara Zajac <kara@soulstone.org>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:57:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] maki: USB through a pipe (shot --usb), real time (--realtime,
 --realtime-from), live console

- A paravirtual pipe at 0x5020_4F00, the end of the USB controller's registers maki's USB
  service maps, where the real controller has nothing: "maki" at +0, then for each channel (0
  serial, 1 FIDO, 2 keyboard) TX, RXAVAIL and RX. maki's USB service built with MAKI_EMU_USB
  carries its serial port, FIDO reports and keystrokes through it.
- `shot --usb PORT` joins the channels to TCP servers on PORT, PORT+1 and PORT+2: maki desktop's
  client reaches the emulated maki on the serial port, python-fido2 on FIDO's 64-byte reports,
  and keystrokes come out as HID usages, printed as text too.
- `--realtime` keeps maki's time from running ahead of this computer's: it sleeps rather than
  skipping idle time (a few milliseconds at a time, the pipe still moving), so a host's timing
  holds (maki-link's link watchdog, CTAPHID's 100 ms between a message's packets). `--realtime-
  from T` paces from instruction count T on, so scripted presses (a PIN) keep their timing.
- `--console-live` prints maki's console as it comes.

